From: itar3 <62651854+itar3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:24:36 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Renderer-specific: shared constant layout, vertex
 pulling, render scale and more

Kept out of the upstream series because they depend on the renderer's
side: constants through XE_* accessors (optional uniform buffers,
XENOS_RECOMP_CONSTANT_BUFFERS), extra shared constants (host base vertex,
render scale, point sprites, tessellation, alpha to mask, sampler filter
overrides) and vertex texture samplers 16-19, vertex pulling for fetches
not indexed by the vertex index, tessellated patch draws, predicated
tiling, the LOD bias in shaders, 1D fetches through 2D views, texel
offsets in guest texels, 7e3 clamping, a NaN debug paint, the
textureFetchMask and shaderFlags cache fields and --blob output.
